# PDF Deck Button Standard

Every button that links to a PDF **must** use the `<Button>` component with `useBaseUrl`. Never use raw `<a>` tags for PDF links.

## Required imports

Every `.mdx` file that contains a PDF button must have these imports at the top (after frontmatter):

```mdx
import useBaseUrl from '@docusaurus/useBaseUrl';
import Button from '@site/src/components/Button';
```

## Component format

```jsx
<Button label="Deck - [Topic the deck addresses]" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/filename.pdf')} />
```

## Label naming

Labels **must** follow the pattern `"Deck - [Topic]"`:

✅ GOOD
```jsx
<Button label="Deck - Genie Best Practices" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/Genie Best Practices.pdf')} />
<Button label="Deck - Genie Spaces Implementation Guide" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/Genie Spaces Implementation Guide.pdf')} />
<Button label="Deck - UC Best Practices" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/UC Best Practices and Patterns from accumulated STS experiences.pdf')} />
<Button label="Deck - Metric Views" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/UC-Metric-Views.pdf')} />
```

❌ BAD — wrong component or wrong label format
```jsx
<a href="/pdfs/file.pdf">View PDF</a>
<Button label="UC Best Practices Deck" ... />
<Button label="View PDF" ... />
```

## Placement

- Place deck buttons inside a `:::tip` admonition (never `:::warning` or `:::danger`).
- Add a short lead-in sentence before the button(s), e.g. "For a more elaborated explanation, check the following deck:"
